`pydict()` first merges `value_types` and `allowed_types` through `_check_signature`, so `(int, str)` plus `(float,)` becomes the normalized sequence `(int, str, float)`. It then calls `_pyiterable(..., variable_nb_elements=False, ...)`, which lowercases those type objects to `['int', 'str', 'float']` and yields one `_random_type(value_types)` result per dictionary value. `_random_type()` chooses one entry from that list, maps it to `pyint`/`pystr`/`pyfloat`, and returns `self.generator.format(...)`; after the earlier `pystruct()` has already advanced the seeded RNG stream, the four `pydict` value draws occur in this exact order.

